<title>DENMARK: Denmark's Great Belt ups bond offer to one bln DKK.</title>
<headline>Denmark's Great Belt ups bond offer to one bln DKK.</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1996-12-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Denmark's Great Belt (A/S Storebaeltsforbindelse) on Thursday raised an existing 750 million crown, four percent, five year bond offer to one billion crowns, lead manager Den Danske Bank said in a statement distributed by Copenhagen Stock Exchange.</p>
<p>The bond matures on December 18, 2001 and the issue was on sale with immediate effect, it said.</p>
<p>The proceeds would be used to finance the building of the Great Belt road-rail-tunnel-bridge fixed link between Denmark's two biggest islands, it added.</p>
<p>--Chris Follett, Copenhagen newsroom +45 33969650</p>
</text>
